  "historical_output_text": " Q: \"How can I clean my wooden cutting board without damaging it?\"\n\nA: To clean your wooden cutting board, start by scraping off any food scraps with a plastic scraper. Next, mix a small amount of mild dish soap with warm water in a basin. Gently scrub the board with a soft-bristled brush, working the soapy water into the wood. Rinse the board thoroughly with clean water, making sure to remove all soap residue. Pat the board dry with a clean cloth and let it air dry. For extra cleaning, you can apply a small amount of mineral oil to the surface, which helps maintain the board's condition. Apply the oil with a soft cloth and buff it in until absorbed. This helps to moisturize the wood and prevent cracking. Avoid using harsh chemicals, hot water, or abrasive sponges, as these can damage the wood",
